{"chunk_id": "3f062de145dc", "text": "This section recounts the birth and early life of Sakuntala and Dushmanta\u2019s son. Raised in the hermitage of the sage Kanwa, the boy grows with extraordinary strength and courage, even subduing wild beasts as a child; the ascetics name him Sarvadamana, \u201cthe subduer of all.\u201d Recognizing the time has come, Kanwa sends Sakuntala and her son to Dushmanta\u2019s court so the child may be acknowledged as heir. When Sakuntala presents the boy, the king publicly denies knowing her or the child. Humiliated but resolute, she delivers a powerful speech on truth, divine witness, marriage, and the sacred duty of a father to recognize his son. The episode is pivotal: it introduces the heroic child (later Bharata) and dramatizes the moral tension between royal power, social reputation, and dharma.\nSakuntala presents her son to King Dushmanta, who denies her; she fiercely rebukes him, asserting truth, dharma, marriage, and the legitimacy of their child.\nThemes: legitimacy and lineage, truth vs denial, dharma and moral witness, power of motherhood, royal responsibility", "vector": [0.021189525723457336, -0.00908410269767046, -0.0043909852392971516, -0.001869861502200365, -0.032012566924095154, 0.017604226246476173, -0.024465978145599365, -0.010574620217084885, -0.030132632702589035, -0.011521301232278347, 0.01725509576499462, 0.003890788881108165, 0.013602654449641705, 0.017429661005735397, -0.004357415251433849, 0.0075063020922243595, 0.04245961830019951, -0.030884604901075363, 0.013058817014098167, -0.025446228682994843, 0.00027338750078342855, -0.02163265272974968, 0.001997428247705102, 0.017349092289805412, -0.028843536972999573, 0.028709255158901215, 0.02897781692445278, -0.029649222269654274, 0.014287487603724003, -0.02768872119486332, -0.011870430782437325, -0.006086281500756741, 0.002440555253997445, -0.021041816100478172, -0.025593938305974007, -0.0025261593982577324, -0.013562370091676712, -0.019672151654958725, 0.01238